WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.377
IN and EXISTS can sometimes be rewritten into equivalent forms.

00:00:04.377 --> 00:00:12.732
But when writing the first version, choose the operator that expresses the business question clearly.

00:00:12.732 --> 00:00:15.612
Membership suggests IN. Existence suggests EXISTS.

00:00:15.612 --> 00:00:19.537
Absence of a related match suggests NOT EXISTS.

00:00:19.537 --> 00:00:24.962
Clear semantics make the query easier to explain, review, and debug.

00:00:24.962 --> 00:00:30.202
EXISTS asks whether at least one related row satisfies the condition.

00:00:30.202 --> 00:00:36.522
The selected columns inside EXISTS usually do not matter; the existence of a row does.

00:00:36.522 --> 00:00:42.672
This maps naturally to questions such as patients with any follow-up, customers with any purchase,

00:00:42.672 --> 00:00:44.766
or orders with no shipment record.
